<fonts>
    <!-- Bahnschrift — Windows' cut of DIN 1451, the German industrial
         standard face off road signs and equipment panels. Subset hard:
         the time font carries only 0-9 and ':', which is what keeps a
         display-size face affordable, and every subset is upper case
         only because nothing on this face is set in lower case.

         Sizes are the cap heights carried over from Clay's approved
         comp — 76px on the time, 24px on the row figures, 14 and 12 on
         the words — re-solved for this typeface. The px that hits a
         given cap is per-face and never transfers.

         The time and the row figures are TABULAR: every digit gets the
         widest digit's advance. Bahnschrift is proportional by default,
         so without it the clock reshuffles every time a 1 rolls past.

         Regenerate with tools/make_din_font.py, one size per screen
         resolution — never scale a bitmap face at runtime. -->
    <font id="dinTime" filename="din_time.fnt" antialias="true"/>
    <font id="dinSmall" filename="din_small.fnt" antialias="true"/>
    <font id="dinLabel" filename="din_label.fnt" antialias="true"/>
    <font id="dinMicro" filename="din_micro.fnt" antialias="true"/>
</fonts>
